# Static-asset headers. THIS FILE — not worker.js — is what actually
# reaches the browser for pages, scripts and styles.
#
# Why: `run_worker_first` is deliberately off in wrangler.toml (turning it
# on caused an outage), so Cloudflare's asset layer serves anything that
# matches a file in public/ WITHOUT invoking the Worker. worker.js's
# addSecurityHeaders() therefore only ever decorates the SPA-fallback
# path — every real page bypassed it and shipped with no CSP, no HSTS
# and no X-Frame-Options. Security audit 2026-08, finding A1.
#
# The Worker copy of these headers is kept in sync deliberately: it still
# covers the fallback path. Change both, or neither.
#
# Note on patterns: Cloudflare requires the splat at the END of a path,
# so `/*.html` never matched anything. `/*` does. HTML still revalidates
# on every load via Cloudflare's default `max-age=0, must-revalidate`.

/*
  X-Content-Type-Options: nosniff
  X-Frame-Options: DENY
  Referrer-Policy: strict-origin-when-cross-origin
  Permissions-Policy: camera=(), microphone=(), geolocation=()
  Strict-Transport-Security: max-age=31536000; includeSubDomains
  Content-Security-Policy: default-src 'self'; script-src 'self' https://esm.sh https://challenges.cloudflare.com; style-src 'self' 'unsafe-inline'; img-src 'self' data:; font-src 'self'; connect-src 'self' https://*.supabase.co https://esm.sh https://challenges.cloudflare.com; frame-src https://challenges.cloudflare.com; frame-ancestors 'none'; base-uri 'self'; form-action 'self'

# Cache policy. Without explicit headers, the browser/edge can serve a
# stale cached module (e.g. /js/shared.js) against a freshly-deployed
# page module, leaving the two out of contract and surfacing as "X is not
# a function" until the user hard-refreshes. `no-cache` keeps the cached
# copy but forces an ETag revalidation on every load — one cheap 304
# round-trip in the steady state, no stale modules across deploys.

/
  Cache-Control: no-cache

/*.html
  Cache-Control: no-cache

/js/*
  Cache-Control: no-cache

/css/*
  Cache-Control: no-cache

/manifest.webmanifest
  Cache-Control: no-cache
